This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   - **Initial request:** "check this session, review all of its work and continue finish what it started, review and merge when done grok --resume 019ff3c7-4795-7f01-83c9-cf3bd38fbaec" — find a `grok` CLI session by UUID, review everything it did, finish the work, review it, and merge.
   - **Follow-up:** "how much change we have done, and did we do the best fix?" — asked for change accounting plus an honest quality assessment.
   - **Follow-up:** "how much code have you changed?" (given as the answer to an AskUserQuestion about the merge gate, i.e. they wanted the number, not the merge decision yet).
   - **Most recent:** "ok do the best fix review and merge" — apply the best available fix, then review and merge.

   The session under review (`019ff3c7…`, model grok-4.5) was itself continuing an opencode session `ses_00e833304ffewmMh5Mm1W5lJfm`. Its work is PR **#2663** `feat(apply): drift gate blocks un-declared remote changes` on branch `feat/apply-drift-gate` in worktree `/Users/burakemre/Code/lobu/.claude/worktrees/apply-drift-gate-continue`. All CI was green except the required `pi-review` status, which had failed 12+ rounds.

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - **Drift gate for `lobu apply`**: fail-closed on un-declared remote state (UI field edits, UI-created definitions) instead of overwriting/auto-deleting under `prune`.
   - **Three-way attribution**: `desired` (config) / `remote` (cloud) / `attribution` (effective remote after last succeeded apply). Converge only when `remote == attribution`; block when `remote ≠ attribution AND desired ≠ remote`.
   - **`owned` set**: kind-qualified incarnation identities (`entity-type:12`, `watcher:b-1`, `connector-definition:5`) that determine delete eligibility. UI-created (unowned) definitions never auto-delete.
   - **Prune-aware facets**: `required`, `properties`, `eventKinds`, `viewTemplate`, `resolutionPolicy` — declared → diff; omitted + prune → removal; omitted + no prune → unmanaged.
   - **Baseline storage**: `{attribution, owned}` inside the deployment event's `payload_data.manifest`, read back via new `GET /api/<org>/deployments/latest`.
   - **Partial index**: `events_succeeded_deployments_idx` on `(organization_id, id DESC) WHERE semantic_type='change' AND metadata->>'category'='deployment' AND metadata->>'status'='succeeded'`, built `CONCURRENTLY` with an INVALID-carcass heal.
   - **`pi-review` gate thresholds** (`docs/REVIEW_SCHEMA.md`): passes only when `bug_free>=80`, `slop<=15`, `simplicity>=70`, `bugs==0`, `blockers==[]`, `tests_adequate==true`. Per-run override: `PI_REVIEW_MIN_SIMPLICITY=<n>`.
   - **`make pre-pr-remote`**: runs 16–18 Linux CI lanes on Depot against the *staged* tree, records a tree-hash attestation that `make review` requires.
   - **Stale dist trap**: `packages/cli/bin/lobu.js` dynamically imports `../dist/index.js` — source edits are invisible to E2E until `bun run build`.

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   - **`packages/cli/src/commands/_lib/apply/diff.ts`** (PR total +965/−30; my delta +136/−41) — the core. Added the single shared projection that replaced three hand-written copies:
     ```ts
     export interface EntityTypeFacets {
       name: string | undefined; description: string | undefined;
       required: string[]; properties: Record<string, unknown>;
       backing: unknown; metrics: unknown; eventKinds: unknown;
       viewTemplate: unknown; schemaExtras: Record<string, unknown>;
     }
     const normalizeEntityFacets = (e): EntityTypeFacets => ({
       name: e.name, description: e.description,
       required: e.required ?? [], properties: e.properties ?? {},
       backing: e.backing, metrics: e.metrics, eventKinds: e.eventKinds,
       viewTemplate: e.viewTemplate, schemaExtras: e.schemaExtras ?? {},
     });
     const remoteEntityTypeFacets = (r: RemoteEntityType): EntityTypeFacets =>
       normalizeEntityFacets(r);

     export const effectiveEntityTypeAfterApply = (
       d: DesiredEntityType, r: RemoteEntityType | undefined, prune: boolean
     ): EntityTypeFacets => {
       const schemaExtras: Record<string, unknown> = {};
       for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(r?.schemaExtras ?? {})) {
         if (prune && key === "x-lobu-resolution" && d.resolutionPolicy === undefined) continue;
         schemaExtras[key] = value;
       }
       if (d.resolutionPolicy) Object.assign(schemaExtras, d.resolutionPolicy);
       const inherit = <T>(declared: T | undefined, live: T | undefined) =>
         declared !== undefined ? declared : prune ? undefined : live;
       const declaredProperties = d.properties;
       const properties =
         declaredProperties === undefined
           ? inherit(undefined, r?.properties)
           : prune ? declaredProperties
           : { ...Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(r?.properties ?? {})
                 .filter(([key]) => !(key in declaredProperties))), ...declaredProperties };
       return normalizeEntityFacets({
         name: d.name !== undefined ? d.name : r?.name,
         description: d.description !== undefined ? d.description : r?.description,
         required: d.required !== undefined ? d.required : prune ? [] : r?.required,
         properties,
         backing: inherit(d.backing, r?.backing),
         metrics: inherit(d.metrics, r?.metrics),
         eventKinds: inherit(d.eventKinds, r?.eventKinds),
         viewTemplate: inherit(d.viewTemplate, r?.viewTemplate),
         schemaExtras,
       });
     };
     export const effectiveRelationshipTypeAfterApply = (d, r): RelationshipTypeFacets => ({
       name: d.name !== undefined ? d.name : r?.name,
       description: d.description !== undefined ? d.description : r?.description,
       rules: d.rules ?? [],
     });
     ```
     Both no-attribution in-sync checks now read:
     ```ts
     const inSync = deepEqual(
       effectiveEntityTypeAfterApply(desired, remote, prune),
       remoteEntityTypeFacets(remote)
     );
     ```
     Deleted `projectEntityForSync` entirely. Made `projectDesiredWatcher` exported. Fixed a biome `useOptionalChain` warning: `baseline?.owned.has(ownedKey("connector-definition", def.id)) ?? false`.
     **UNCOMMITTED change:** `projectRemoteWatcher` now normalizes `name: w.name ?? null` (was `w.name`) with a comment explaining the `deepEqual(null, undefined)` asymmetry.

   - **`packages/cli/src/commands/_lib/apply/deployment.ts`** (my delta +52/−113). `buildAttributionAndOwned` entity/relationship/watcher blocks collapsed to:
     ```ts
     const entityTypes = state.memorySchema.entityTypes.map((d) => {
       const r = remoteEntityBySlug.get(d.slug);
       return { id: r?.id, slug: d.slug, ...effectiveEntityTypeAfterApply(d, r, prune) };
     });
     const relationshipTypes = state.memorySchema.relationshipTypes.map((d) => {
       const r = remoteRelBySlug.get(d.slug);
       return { id: r?.id, slug: d.slug, ...effectiveRelationshipTypeAfterApply(d, r) };
     });
