       const r = remoteWatcherBySlug.get(d.slug);
       const p = projectDesiredWatcher(d, r);
       return { slug: d.slug, behavior_id: r?.behavior_id, agent_id: p.agent, name: p.name,
         description: p.description, prompt: p.prompt, triggers: p.triggers, skills: p.skills,
         sources: p.sources, reactions_guidance: p.reactionsGuidance,
         device_worker_id: p.deviceWorkerId, notification_channel: p.notificationChannel,
         notification_priority: p.notificationPriority, min_cooldown_seconds: p.minCooldownSeconds,
         tags: p.tags, agent_kind: p.agentKind, outputs: p.outputs, classifiers: p.classifiers };
     });
     ```
     Added `toBaseline(record: BaselineRecord | null): Baseline` next to `loadBaselineFromManifest`.

   - **`packages/cli/src/commands/_lib/apply/apply-cmd.ts`** (my delta +55/−92). Extracted `recordableBaseline(snapshot: RemoteSnapshot): BaselineRecord` (deduped the `--only` carry-forward rules that existed twice); `let baselineRecordForRecording = recordableBaseline(remote);` and post-apply `baselineRecordForRecording = recordableBaseline(postRemote);`. Collapsed `pins` ternary. Simplified template-fetch guard to `if (desired?.viewTemplate === undefined && !prune) continue;`. Replaced 23-line cast block with `const baseline = toBaseline(baselineRecord);`.

   - **`packages/cli/src/commands/_lib/apply/client.ts`** (my delta +16/−5). `getLatestDeployment` wrapped in try/catch returning `null` on `ApiError` with `status === 404`, propagating everything else.

   - **`packages/cli/src/commands/_lib/apply/__tests__/diff-baseline.test.ts`** (my delta +134). 6 new tests: relationship omitted-name in-sync → noop; declared rule change still blocks; prune + remote-only eventKinds/viewTemplate → blocks; no-prune + eventKinds → noop; prune + UI-added property → blocks; nameless remote Behavior + omitted config name → noop.

   - **`packages/cli/src/commands/_lib/apply/__tests__/client.test.ts`** (+29). Two tests in a new `describe("ApplyClient — deployment baseline read")`: 404 → null, 500 → throws.

   - **`packages/server/src/lobu/__tests__/deployment-routes.test.ts`** — restored `origin/main` version verbatim and appended only the new `describe('blocked deployments + GET /deployments/latest')` block in repo style (2-space, single quotes), using the top-level imported `authStash` rather than a dynamic re-import. Went from +585/−404 to **+143/−0**.

   - **`docs/plans/lobu-apply-drift-gate.md`** — Status line now "v1 shipped in PR #2663"; added a "### What actually shipped (PR #2663 — PR-1 + PR-2 + PR-3 combined)" section listing shipped vs deferred (`--confirm-deletes` token, `--bootstrap`, adopt codegen); replaced all "exit 1" prose with non-zero / `2` (the CLI's `ValidationError` code).

   - **`db/migrations/20260812010000_events_succeeded_deployments_idx.sql`** (unchanged by me) — verified live: index exists, `EXPLAIN` shows `Index Scan using events_succeeded_deployments_idx` with only `organization_id` as Index Cond.

4. **Errors and fixes:**
   - **First E2E run used stale `dist`.** `packages/cli/bin/lobu.js` dynamically imports `../dist/index.js`. Detected because the recorded attribution lacked `required: []` that my normalization guarantees. Fixed with `cd packages/cli && bun run build`, then re-ran everything.
   - **E2E auto-apply failed** with `provider "mock" does not exist`. Fixed by switching the scratch config to the `gemini` provider with a fake key.
   - **`lobu apply -c local` → "unknown option '-c'".** `apply` takes `--url`, not `-c`; used `--url http://localhost:9473`.
   - **Depot gate run 3 failed on 3 lanes**, none from the diff: `server-integration-bun` had 1 failure in 1834 (`OAuthStateStore (Postgres-backed)` beforeEach/afterEach timeout at 5000ms — passes locally in 3.18s), `integration` is its aggregate, and `dead-code-report` never ran an attempt ("Cancelled due to the workflow concurrency policy"). Verified knip locally (`bun run knip --include files` — clean) and re-ran the gate: all 18 lanes passed.
   - **First `make review` picked codex, which died** on `Network is unreachable (os error 51)` / DNS failure to `wss://chatgpt.com/backend-api/codex/responses` after 200,622 tokens. Confirmed network was fine afterwards; re-ran with `REVIEWER_CLI=claude CLAUDE_REVIEW_MODEL=fable` per the stored preference (Fable is the designated advisor model; never Sonnet).
   - **Biome format error** after reorganizing client tests into a new describe — fixed with `bunx biome check --write` on that file.
   - **`TS6133: 'Baseline' is declared but its value is never read`** in apply-cmd.ts after introducing `toBaseline` — removed the now-unused type import.
   - **Two `make pre-pr-remote` runs killed by me** because I kept editing the tree after starting them (the attestation is tree-hash bound). Lesson applied: settle the tree first.

5. **Problem Solving:**
   - Diagnosed that both remaining pi-review blockers shared one root cause: three hand-written copies of the apply's write semantics (entity in-sync check, relationship in-sync check, `buildAttributionAndOwned`). Fixed the class, not the instances — per the repo's own invariant "Fix the class, not the instance" and "never mirror an encoding".
