   - Determined that unifying `diffEntityType` (two-way) with `compareEntityTypeThreeWay` (three-way) is **NOT a safe refactor**: they genuinely differ on `name`/`description` (two-way flags omitted values via `stringChanged`, three-way filters them as unmanaged) and on `backing`/`metrics` (two-way always-managed, three-way filtered outside prune), and the two-way path is live for rollback (`computeDiff(sanitized.state, remote, {})` — no baseline) and creates.
