1	/**
2	 * Revolut Connector
3	 *
4	 * Revolut has no public personal-banking API, so the transactions feed reads
5	 * the user's history by REPLAYING the retail API the Revolut web app
6	 * (`app.revolut.com`) already calls — not by scraping the rendered DOM. It runs
7	 * inside the user's real signed-in Chrome via the paired Owletto extension:
8	 * reuse the revolut.com sticky anchor the user signs into once, capture the app's own
9	 * `transactions/last` request headers, then page the FULL history in-page by
10	 * walking the `?to=<cursor>` parameter and parsing each
11	 * `GET /api/retail/user/current/transactions/last` JSON page.
12	 *
13	 * Why replay, not scrape: the previous DOM-scrape path parsed amounts out of
14	 * rendered row text, which broke against Revolut's virtualized SPA and produced
15	 * corrupt amounts (a coffee read as £180,611). The retail API returns `amount`
16	 * as a signed integer in MINOR units (−£23.45 = `-2345`); dividing by
17	 * 10^exponent is exact and kills the decimal-parse corruption entirely.
18	 *
19	 * Why replay, not scroll: Revolut's list only fetches older `?to=` pages on a
20	 * real wheel scroll, which a non-rendered/automated tab can't reproduce (the CDP
21	 * wheel is frame-throttled and never acks). But the retail API is plain JSON
22	 * paginated by a `?to=<epoch_ms>` cursor — so once we have the app's request
23	 * headers we can fetch every older page directly, in-page, no scrolling. The one
24	 * non-reconstructible header (`x-device-id`, an in-memory app token — NOT the
25	 * localStorage tracker id) is captured by wrapping fetch/XHR and forcing one
26	 * real app request via a SPA route remount; the captured set replays cleanly on
27	 * new `?to=` URLs (the API is not per-request signed). A same-origin in-page
28	 * `fetch` carries cookies (`credentials:"include"`) plus those headers, so it
29	 * authenticates where a header-less raw fetch 401s (`{code:9001}`).
30	 *
31	 * The balances feed uses the authenticated Invest app instead. It joins stable
32	 * account ids from the app's `trading/accounts` response to selected cells in
33	 * the rendered portfolio tables, and rejects snapshots that fail its account
34	 * and total-value completeness checks rather than storing raw page text.
35	 *
36	 * Transaction auth is implicit but two-layered: SSO login ≠ retail-API auth.
37	 * The app-level passcode (rwa flow) must be entered in app.revolut.com or the
38	 * retail API 401s (`{code:9001}`) and the page renders skeletons. When that
39	 * happens — no transactions intercepted — we `notifyRevolutAuthWall` and throw
40	 * `RevolutAuthWallError` instead of reporting a silently-empty sync.
41	 *
42	 * The transaction event shape matches the original file-import Revolut
43	 * connector (`semantic_type: "transaction"`, metadata `{ date, description,
44	 * amount, direction, balance, currency }`) so historical imports stay uniform.
45	 */
